// string_concat_null — Phase 11 Q4 made null arithmetic a compile error.
// This test previously pinned the Phase 8e-9a "known limitation" that
// "x" + null evaluated the null literal as int 0 and concatenated "0"
// ("x0", exit 2). With the null sentinel now surviving implicit
// coercion, the raw 0 would silently concatenate an arbitrary pool
// string — worse than a diagnostic — so the operand is rejected at
// compile time (see ExprResolver Access(SnBinaryExpr)).
int main() {
    string s = "x" + null;
    return s.length();
}
